@display("std/grammar")
grammar: part {
  | A language's grammar as a surface of the contract [layer](#heron.language.specifications.layers.layer): its productions and tokens, in a notation whose operators are `|`, `?`, `*`, `+` and grouping. A spec that describes a language imports it; the core kinds of a spec don't need it.
  |
  | | Kind                        | Holds                                     |
  | | --------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
  | | `grammar(notation)`         | `start`, productions and tokens, and the file `@source` keeps it equal to |
  | | `production`                | a named rule and its expression, verbatim |
  | | `token`                     | a terminal, by its pattern or literal      |

  grammar_kind: term {{
    `@source("…") name: grammar(notation = …) { … }`, a language's syntax as productions
    and tokens whose text is kept verbatim. `@source` names a file the grammar is kept equal to.
  }}

  @by(system.checker)
  @targets(grammar_kind)
  grammar_layer: rule {
    must {{ give `grammar`, `production` and `token` the `CONTRACT` [layer](#language.specifications.layers.layer), each production and token an entry of the grammar's surface }}
  }

  @by(system.docs_generator)
  @targets(grammar_kind)
  grammar_view: rule {
    must {{ show each production with every name in its text linked to the production or token it names, and under each the productions that use it }}
  }

  @by(system.docs_generator)
  @targets(grammar_kind)
  grammar_source: rule {
    where {{ a grammar names a `@source` }}
    must {{ fail the spec's grammar test unless the grammar's productions and tokens equal the source's }}
  }
}
